.TH GITM8 1 "June 2026" "gitm8" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gitm8 \- terminal dashboard for common Git workflows
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY gitm8
.YS
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B gitm8
is a small terminal user interface for day-to-day Git work.
It opens an interactive dashboard for reviewing changes, staging and unstaging
files, committing, fetching, pulling, pushing, syncing, switching branches,
rebasing, viewing logs, opening pull requests, and switching repository-local
Git identity profiles.
.PP
.B gitm8
does not reimplement Git storage or transport.
It shells out to the installed
.BR git (1)
binary, so existing Git configuration, hooks, SSH keys, credential helpers,
commit signing, aliases used by Git itself, and repository settings remain in
effect.
.PP
Run
.B gitm8
from inside the repository you want to work on.
If launched outside a Git worktree, Git-backed actions fail in the same way the
corresponding
.BR git (1)
command would fail.
.SH DASHBOARD
The screen contains a repository status bar, a Git output area, a changed-files
panel, a preview/review/log panel, and a footer with key bindings.
The top bar shows repository name, current branch, configured Git user,
upstream, ahead/behind counts, staged and unstaged counts, last fetch time, and
the active viewer mode.
.PP
The dashboard opens on the first changed file when changes are present.
Press
.B d
to toggle the selected file between content preview and diff preview.
Press
.B 0
to show the repository-wide review.
File previews include lightweight theme-aware syntax highlighting for common
source and configuration file types.
.SS Keys
.TP
.B Up, Down
Move the file, branch, profile, or picker selection.
.TP
.B Enter
Preview the selected file, accept the selected picker item, or confirm an
active text input.
.TP
.B 0
Show repository-wide review.
.TP
.B d
Toggle the selected file between diff and content preview.
.TP
.B s, S
Stage the selected file, or stage all changes.
.TP
.B u, U
Unstage the selected file, or unstage all changes.
.TP
.B c
Commit staged changes.
Inside the commit prompt,
.B Ctrl-g
asks the configured AI CLI to generate a commit message from staged changes and
populate the input.
.TP
.B f
Fetch all remotes and prune stale remote-tracking refs.
.TP
.B p, P
Pull with fast-forward only mode, or push.
.TP
.B x
Sync by pulling with rebase, then pushing.
.TP
.B b
Open the branch switcher.
.TP
.B l
View recent commit logs.
.TP
.B r, Ctrl-p
Open pull request options for the current branch using
.BR gh (1) .
Choose
.B g
to generate a title and body with the configured AI provider, or
.B m
to write the pull request yourself in
.BR "gh pr create" .
.B gitm8
does not push while creating a pull request; push the branch first.
.TP
.B R, Ctrl-r
Open the rebase picker.
.TP
.B i
Switch repository-local Git identity profile.
.TP
.B h
Open help.
.TP
.B o
Expand or collapse the Git output box.
.TP
.B Tab
Hide or show the footer key bar.
.TP
.B y
Open
.BR yazi (1),
if installed.
.TP
.B j, k
Scroll the viewer line by line.
.TP
.B PageDown, PageUp, Ctrl-f, Ctrl-b
Scroll the viewer by a page.
.TP
.B g, G
Jump the viewer to the top or bottom.
.TP
.B q, Ctrl-c
Quit.
.SH BRANCHES
In the branch switcher, use
.B Up
and
.B Down
to choose a branch,
.B Enter
to switch to it,
.B W
to switch while carrying current changes through stash/pop,
.B n
to create a branch,
.B D
to delete the selected branch, and
.B Esc
to return to review mode.
.PP
The branch list shows local branches followed by remote-only branches.
Remote branches are de-duplicated and shown without their remote prefix.
.SH REBASE
In the rebase picker, use
.B Up
and
.B Down
to choose a target branch and
.B Enter
to rebase the current branch onto it.
If a rebase is already in progress, use
.B c
to continue,
.B a
to abort, or
.B s
to skip the current patch.
.PP
If the rebase stops on conflicts, resolve them with normal Git commands outside
.BR gitm8 ,
then continue from the dashboard or by running
.BR "git rebase --continue" .
.SH CONFIGURATION
Configuration is loaded from
.IR ~/.gitm8rc ,
then
.IR ~/.gitm8/credentials .
Environment variables override defaults.
.TP
.B GITM8_DEFAULT_BRANCH
Default branch name.
Default:
.BR main .
.TP
.B GITM8_EDITOR
Editor used by workflows that need one.
Default:
.B EDITOR
or
.BR vi .
.TP
.B GITM8_THEME
Dashboard color theme.
.TP
.B GITM8_CONFIRM_DESTRUCTIVE_ACTIONS
Whether destructive actions should ask for confirmation where applicable.
.TP
.B GITM8_FETCH_ON_STARTUP
Fetch from all remotes with pruning before the dashboard opens.
.TP
.B GITM8_SHOW_COMMIT_GRAPH
Show graph lines in the commit log view.
.TP
.B GITM8_AI_PROVIDER
AI CLI used for generated commit messages and pull request text.
Supported values:
.B codex
and
.BR claude .
Default:
.BR codex .
.SH THEMES
Built-in themes:
.PP
.EX
amber
catppuccin
catppuccin-frappe
catppuccin-latte
catppuccin-macchiato
catppuccin-mocha
cyan
default
forest
highvis
lime
midnight
mono
ocean
rose
steel
violet
.EE
.PP
.B catppuccin
maps to
.BR catppuccin-mocha .
.SH PROFILES
Define switchable Git identities in
.IR ~/.gitm8/profiles ,
one per line:
.PP
.EX
Work     = Ada Lovelace <ada@work.example>
Personal = Ada <ada@personal.example>
.EE
.PP
Selecting a profile runs
.B git config user.name
and
.B git config user.email
for the current repository only.
The global Git identity is left untouched.
.SH DEPENDENCIES
.TP
.BR git (1)
Required. All repository operations use the installed Git binary.
.TP
.BR gh (1)
Required for pull-request creation and viewing.
Authenticate with
.B gh auth login
before using the dashboard pull-request key.
.TP
.BR codex (1)
Optional. Default AI provider for generated commit messages and pull request
text.
.TP
.BR claude (1)
Optional. Used only when
.B GITM8_AI_PROVIDER
is set to
.BR claude .
.TP
.BR yazi (1)
Optional. Used only when pressing
.B y
in the dashboard.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The dashboard exited successfully.
.TP
.B 2
Unsupported command-line arguments were provided.
.TP
.B non-zero
The dashboard failed to start or exited with an error.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Open the dashboard in the current repository:
.EX
cd path/to/project
gitm8
.EE
.TP
Open the dashboard with a specific theme:
.EX
GITM8_THEME=catppuccin gitm8
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR git (1),
.BR gh (1),
.BR codex (1),
.BR claude (1),
.BR yazi (1)
.SH BUGS
Report issues at
.UR https://github.com/b404dev/gitm8/issues
.UE .
